--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DEAD CODE — REMOVED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

[REMOVED] toggleCompactMode() — inert try/catch (was ~line 20910-20915)
  Original:
      // Resize window for compact mode
      try {
          console.log('Compact mode activated - content optimized for minimal space');
      } catch (error) {
          console.log('Could not resize PiP window:', error);
      }
  Why dead: the try body is a single console.log with a static string — it
  cannot throw, so the catch branch is unreachable. The comment ("Resize
  window for compact mode") doesn't match what the code does (nothing is
  resized). Pure debug leftover with no observable effect.
  Action: deleted both branches.

[REMOVED] adjustPipWindowSize(pipWindow, content) — whole function (was
  ~line 20919-20937) + its only call site (was ~line 20697-20700, a
  setTimeout wrapper in the PiP-open flow).
  Original function computed `optimalWidth` / `optimalHeight` from the
  content's scroll dimensions and then only console.log'd them — the values
  were never applied to anything (no window.resizeTo, no style write). The
  function's own comment admits why: "The Document Picture-in-Picture API
  doesn't support dynamic resizing." So the function did real work
  (layout reads + arithmetic) purely to produce a debug log line that
  nothing consumed.
  Action: deleted the function and the setTimeout(() => adjustPipWindowSize
  (...), 100) call site that invoked it.

Net: 32 lines removed, syntax-checked clean afterward (`node -c`).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. LOOKED DEAD BUT ARE NOT — LEFT ALONE (do not remove)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A grep-based "declared but only referenced once" scan flagged three
functions as apparently unused inside AttendanceTimeCheckerPlus.js. Each
was individually verified against the project's test/dev tooling before
being ruled out — none should be deleted:

  - updateSnakeGame() (line ~5834 pre-cleanup)
    Comment above it: "Kept so any stray caller from v1 still resolves."
    This is a deliberate backward-compatibility shim, kept on purpose.

  - snakeFreeRegionConnected() (line ~5321 pre-cleanup)
    Has zero callers inside the userscript itself, but is exercised by
    snake-dev/snake-verify.js (`S.snakeFreeRegionConnected(walls, wrap)`),
    which flood-fills every stage in SNAKE_STAGES at test time to catch an
    unwinnable sealed-off pocket before it ships. Load-bearing test
    infrastructure, not dead code.

  - cyberTextContrast() (line ~19261 pre-cleanup)
    Same story: unused inside the userscript, but asserted directly by
    cyber-dev/cyber-verify.js (`m.cyberTextContrast() > 4.5` / `< 3`) as
    part of the WCAG contrast checks for the Cyberpunk HUD palette.

Lesson for any future pass: a "no callers in this file" grep is not
sufficient for this repo — always also grep the matching `*-dev/*verify*.js`
/ `*-dev/load.js` before deleting anything that looks orphaned.

