3. COMMENTS — AUDITED, NONE REMOVED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Searched for boilerplate/restate-the-code comments (e.g. "// increment i"
above `i++`), stale TODO/FIXME/HACK markers, and disabled code kept in
`//`/`/* */` blocks. Result: none of substance. The comments in this file
are overwhelmingly rationale/history notes (why a value is what it is, what
regression a check prevents, what a v1 bug looked like) rather than
redundant restatements, so there was nothing safe to cut here without
losing real information. Examples deliberately left in place: the
BUILD_SEED/BUILD_LABEL block at the top (release-process instructions), and
the assorted "legacy scalar" comments around lines 620-1675/5188-5497
(explain why an old storage key is still being read).

